    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d444">

                <pb facs="0340" n="336" sameAs="frus:frus1938v04/pg336"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.1164 University of Shanghai/29:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Shanghai</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Lochhart</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-06-01T22:00:00+08:00">June 1, 1938—10
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received June 1—5:15 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>753. My No. 644, May 11, 4 p.m.<anchor n="36" xml:id="d444-f1"/> Reference
                    paragraph 3 regarding the return of the property of the American Southern
                    Baptist Mission on Paohsing Road.</p>
                <p>I am pleased to report that the above-mentioned property was formally returned by
                    the Japanese authorities to the mission this morning in the presence of the
                    treasurer and two other representatives of the mission, representatives of the
                    Japanese military and consular authorities and a representative of this
                    office.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Hankow, Peiping and Tokyo.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lockhart</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
